Subject: [PATCH 2/9] geph5-misc-rpc: dual-mode control-socket resolution on Android

Android has no writable /run, so the unix default of /run/geph/control.sock
cannot be created. The socket now resolves through android_state_dir(), a
runtime resolver shared with platform.rs's state_dir(): the
root/KernelSU-Magisk module gets /data/adb/geph5, an unprivileged Termux
service (termux-services/runit, packaged by android/termux/) gets
$HOME/.geph5, and GEPH5_STATE_DIR overrides both for tests and rescue
shells. Sharing one resolver means the socket can never drift away from the
state it describes.

This forced MANAGER_CONTROL_SOCK from a const into manager_control_sock(),
so the patch now also touches its two call sites (the transport dialer in
this file; serve_manager in platform.rs). Fragility stays low: the
resolution logic is an additive cfg arm, and conflicts only arrive if
upstream restructures the socket constants themselves.

android_state_dir() needs libc::geteuid(); the android-only libc dependency
lives in patch 0007.
